# What is a subnet mask?
A subnet mask is a 32-bit number that divides an IP address into network and host portions. It is used to determine which part of an IP address belongs to the network and which part belongs to the host.
## What a subnet mask does?
A subnet mask helps in identifying the network and host portions of an IP address, enabling devices to communicate within the same network segment.
## what does /24 means?
The "/24" notation indicates that the first 24 bits of the subnet mask are set to 1, and the remaining 8 bits are set to 0. This corresponds to a subnet mask of 255.255.255.0.
## What is the difference between a network address and a broadcast address?
A network address is the unique identifier for a network segment, while a broadcast address is used to send messages to all devices within that segment.
